{
 "text": "If you skip leg day, you're not skipping one workout. You're skipping more than half your muscle. Your lower body holds over half your skeletal muscle. That's your biggest growth engine… and Max left it parked. Mistake one: 'I squat, so I'm good.' Nope. After ten weeks of squats, quads and glutes grew. Hamstrings didn't. Add Romanian deadlifts or leg curls. Mistake two: three sets and done. Ten or more hard sets per muscle, every week, grows more than fewer than five. Mistake three: one leg day a week. Split it into two. Training a muscle twice a week beats once. Save this for your next leg day… or end up like Max.",
